{"id":"drink-offering","name":"Drink Offering","aliases":[],"sources":["nave","torrey","easton"],"topics":["nave:drink-offering","torrey:drink-offering"],"groups":[],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Drink-offering","text":"Consisted of wine (Num. 15:5; Hos. 9:4) poured around the altar (Ex. 30:9). Joined with meat-offerings (Num. 6:15, 17; 2 Kings 16:13; Joel 1:9, 13; 2:14), presented daily (Ex. 29:40), on the Sabbath (Num. 28:9), and on feast-days (28:14). One-fourth of an hin of wine was required for one lamb, one-third for a ram, and one-half for a bullock (Num. 15:5; 28:7, 14). “Drink offerings of blood” (Ps. 16:4) is used in allusion to the heathen practice of mingling the blood of animals sacrificed with wine or water, and pouring out the mixture in the worship of the gods, and the idea conveyed is that the psalmist would not partake of the abominations of the heathen."},"lemmas":[{"strong":"H5262","lemma":"נֶסֶךְ","xlit":"neçek","gloss":"a libation","kjv":"cover, drink offering, molten image","count":18,"share":0.58},{"strong":"H5258","lemma":"נָסַךְ","xlit":"nâçak","gloss":"to pour out, especially a libation, or to cast","kjv":"cover, melt, offer, pour","count":9,"share":0.29},{"strong":"H1969","lemma":"הִין","xlit":"hîyn","gloss":"a hin or liquid measure","kjv":"hin","count":8,"share":0.26},{"strong":"H4503","lemma":"מִנְחָה","xlit":"minchâh","gloss":"a donation","kjv":"gift, oblation, offering, present","count":9,"share":0.29},{"strong":"H6241","lemma":"עִשָּׂרוֹן","xlit":"ʻissârôwn","gloss":"a tenth part","kjv":"tenth deal","count":5,"share":0.16},{"strong":"H4446","lemma":"מְלֶכֶת","xlit":"mᵉleketh","gloss":"a queen","kjv":"queen","count":4,"share":0.13}],"verses":["Gen.35.14","Exod.29.40","Exod.30.9","Lev.23.13","Num.15.5","Num.15.7","Num.15.10","Ps.16.4","Isa.57.6","Jer.7.18","Jer.19.13","Jer.44.17","Jer.44.18","Jer.44.19","Ezek.20.28","Ezek.45.17","Joel.1.9","Joel.1.13","Num.15.3","Num.15.4","Num.15.6","Num.15.8","Num.15.9","Deut.32.37","Deut.3